# Role
You are the Band-side host of TinyWins' two Goal Room agents
(`services/band-worker/main.py`). The web service stays the source of
truth; you only relay @mentions to it as HMAC-signed callbacks and voice
its replies back into the room. Runs wherever the six env vars exist
(locally during the build; the `tinywins-band` Render worker in prod).

# Requirements
Python, `band-sdk`. Two agents via `Agent.create(adapter, agent_id,
api_key)` run concurrently with `asyncio.gather`:

- **Goal Coach** (`BAND_COACH_AGENT_ID`/`BAND_COACH_API_KEY`), adapter
  mirrors each mention to `/api/internal/band/coach-event` and replies
  with a short acknowledgment.
- **Reflection Guide** (`BAND_REFLECTION_*`), adapter parses message
  content as JSON (falling back to `{"content": <formatted text>}` for
  human free text), posts it to `/api/internal/band/reflections`, and
  **voices the web's `reply` field** into the room — falling back to a
  short "received" line if the response has no reply.

All user-facing replies use `tools.send_message` (a normal chat bubble).
`send_event` types (thought/error) are hidden behind Band's event-type
filter — never put the reply a human is waiting for inside one.

Band's API rejects agent messages with zero mentions — every reply must
mention the triggering sender via `mentions=[{"id": msg.sender_id}]` (the
id-bearing dict is the SDK's ground-truth shape that cannot miss the
participants cache). Configure `logging.basicConfig` at startup
(`BAND_LOG_LEVEL`, default INFO) so SDK/adapter errors reach the process
log instead of vanishing into handlerless loggers.

`post_internal(path, payload)` signs the JSON body with HMAC-SHA256
(`INTERNAL_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, hex digest in `X-TinyWins-Signature`), POSTs
to `TINY_WINS_WEB_URL` + path, and returns the parsed response JSON.

Resilience: a web-service failure must produce a labeled "can't reach
TinyWins right now" thought event, never an adapter crash — the agents
must keep answering mentions while the web side is down. Every required
env var missing at startup is a hard, named error.

# Dependencies
`services/band-worker/requirements.txt` (band-sdk). Counterpart contract:
`prompts/band_callbacks_typescript.prompt`.

# Acceptance criteria (manual, worker has no test harness)
- Both agents connect and stay connected with valid credentials.
- A human free-text @mention to Reflection Guide yields a visible chat
  message in the room (real reply with the LLM up, labeled offline line
  with it down) — never silence, never a filtered-away thought.
- A structured check-in mention yields the persisted-reflection reply as
  a chat message.
- Stopping the web service makes mentions produce a labeled
  "can't reach TinyWins" chat message; restarting restores replies.
